# Extract and single responsibility

Prefer readable modules over god files. Behavior-preserving extract first; do not rewrite while splitting.

## When to extract

1. File grows past ~400 lines, or a function clearly does more than one job → split before new feature work.
2. Pure helpers → `lib/<domain>/`. UI state/handlers → hooks or components in the same domain folder.
3. Mirror existing domain layout (`components/<domain>/`, `lib/<domain>/`) instead of dumping at repo root.

## Do not copy-paste pipelines

- Reuse existing sync/hydrate/upload modules (`lib/db/*`, `lib/gallery/*`, `lib/storage/*`, `lib/image-pipeline/*`).
- Do **not** invent a fourth photo upload path or duplicate `getX`/`syncX` blocks — extend the shared helper.
- When two paths look similar but differ on purpose (e.g. Gallery save vs `gallery-loose-save`), keep both and document; do not force-merge without an explicit product ask.

## Safe refactor default

Move code + re-export stable import paths. No API contract, store shape, or UX changes unless the user asks.
